Usage: truncate OPTION... FILE...

Shrink or extend the size of each FILE to the specified size.

A FILE argument that does not exist is created.

Mandatory arguments to long options are mandatory for short options too.

SIZE is an integer and optional unit (example: 10M is 10*1024*1024).
Units are K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y (powers of 1024) or KB, MB,... (powers of 1000).

SIZE may also be prefixed with +, -, <, >, /, or % for GNU-style
relative, clamp, and rounding adjustments. -o treats SIZE as file-system
I/O blocks.

OPTIONS:
  -c, --no-create      do not create files
  -o, --io-blocks      treat SIZE as number of IO blocks
  -s, --size ARG       set or adjust the file size by SIZE bytes
  -r, --reference ARG  base size on RFILE
      --help           display this help and exit
  -V, --version        output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
